{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/20194-donating-rpg-books-for-the-holidays","id":20194,"title":"Donating RPG books for the holidays","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-29T08:14:48-08:00","id":20194,"title":"Donating RPG books for the holidays","content":"I had an idea. Since we are in the Christmas season, I have lots of old RPG books that I can give away during the holidays. Is there a forum where we can give some old White Wolf or other RPG's to families in need?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T08:43:44-08:00","id":20202,"title":"","content":"I don't think CCP or OPP is really set up to easily do that on any kind of an organized basis. I doubt they'd have a problem with you setting up a thread going &quot;need these books and can't afford 'em?&quot; However, I can also suggest looking around your local area for an organization that would benefit from them, such as troubled teen centers or if all else fails the public library. Getting games more publicly accessible in general helps all around. This is particularly true if you volunteer to run some interesting games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T11:41:55-08:00","id":20265,"title":"","content":"There are groups out there who collect games for our troops. A quick Google search should pull them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T12:33:12-08:00","id":20297,"title":"","content":"I am not sure if churches (yes, some churches think that roleplaying games are evil) but check with the local charity that sends care packages to the troops. Active duty guys have to do something when they are not on alert. I played D&amp;D when I was stationed in Korea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T21:55:26-08:00","id":20504,"title":"","content":"When I was in the sandbox someone sent us Mage Knights minis. I appreciated my fellow gamers thinking of us overseas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"